From 51356535cdd93723b149ac0d7cff19c73a98d187 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:33:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 46/51] Sync the word book into Maimemo's cloud notepad

The word book now pushes into the Maimemo open API: entering the
token in the learning center verifies it and creates (or finds) the
account's private "BiPipe" cloud notepad, and the sync button on
the word book page appends every unsynced word to it. Confirmed
words carry a lit checkmark on their card.

The sync is incremental and idempotent: the notepad's content is
read first and only missing lines are appended, so re-syncing never
duplicates. Every line is written with Maimemo's // prefix, which
maps inflected forms (looked, running - exactly what tapping
subtitles collects) back to their base form, the correct thing to
actually memorize. Confirmation re-reads the notepad after a settle
pause (the server parses content asynchronously, verified against
the live API) and counts a word as confirmed when it appears in the
parsed list, as its base form, or simply as a written line; words
the dictionary does not know stay unsynced and are reported.

The API response shape was verified live before writing any code:
every reply is wrapped in an {errors, data, success} envelope (not
in the OpenAPI document), the private notepad status is
UNPUBLISHED, and an empty notepad content is rejected - the
notepad is therefore created with a placeholder line.

The token, the synced marks and their timestamps live in the
default shared preferences, so they ride along in every data
export and cloud backup without any backup-side change.
